 "subject": "grove,ranking,mcp,cli: remove embedding fallback, fail closed on no-terms",
 "body": "Grove's embedding-based semantic search is gone (companion commit in\ngrove b40b72d9 \u2014 see it for the measurement: an agent guessing one\nkeyword through lexical search beats it in 12/15 cases). This is the\nprism-side removal plus the fix it forced: prism_query's no-terms path\nused to fall back to that same embedding search, silently. It no\nlonger falls back to anything \u2014 a call with no terms now fails closed\nwith guidance to guess a keyword or grep/prism_search first. Same\ndiscipline mason's own harness already enforced (code_context requires\nterms); this closes the gap for every OTHER MCP client and the Bash\nCLI, which could still omit it.\n\nA second, larger consumer surfaced during this: Grove's semantic\nsimilarity fed the general-purpose ranker (internal/ranking) on EVERY\nprism_query/prism_task call, not just the no-terms case \u2014 weighted\n10-25% of the composite delivery score across all 4 profiles, with a\npersisted per-repo learning loop (internal/ranking/learned_weights.go)\nthat reinforced its weight from real usage. RelevanceThreshold (0.15)\nis an ABSOLUTE cutoff a symbol's score is compared against to decide\ndelivery fidelity, so simply zeroing the signal would have silently\nsh",
